### 2. `commands.sh` (कमांड्स ऑटोमेट करण्यासाठी)

ही फाईल **`commands.sh`** नावाने सेव्ह करून थेट टर्मिनलवर `bash commands.sh` मारून सगळा सेटअप चालवू शकता.

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "========================================="
echo "   Kubernetes Deployment & Service Setup "
echo "========================================="

# 1. Apply Deployment Manifest
echo "[1/4] Deploying 4 Nginx Pods..."
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

# 2. Apply Service Manifest
echo "[2/4] Exposing Service via NodePort 30080..."
kubectl apply -f service.yaml

# 3. Wait for Pods to be Ready
echo "[3/4] Waiting for pods to enter Running state..."
sleep 5
kubectl get pods -o wide

# 4. Verify NodePort Service
echo "[4/4] Fetching Service Details..."
kubectl get svc hostname-service

echo ""
echo "========================================="
echo "        Testing Load Balancing           "
echo "========================================="
for i in {1..4}
do
   echo -n "Request $i: "
   curl -s http://localhost:30080
done

echo ""
echo "Done! Refreshing will change the Pod IP dynamically."
